# Shell scripts are executed on a Linux server. Git's autocrlf turns their line
# endings into CRLF in the working tree on Windows, and scp copies them across
# verbatim -- where bash reads `set -u\r` as an invalid option and every
# function definition as a syntax error. The failure appears only on the server,
# and only after the file has been edited from Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
